-- title:
--   Unit criterion at an end of the blown-up supersingular chart
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Further, $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((t))$ (`LaurentSeries L`) which by `hK` equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield of $L((t))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Next, $A$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra, compatibly with $L$. The element $j\in K$ is nonzero and its Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant (`hj`); $\varpi\in A$ generates $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and $X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the scheme obtained as the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}C_\infty$ (where $C_\infty$ consists of the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$) along the common middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and canonical morphism $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}:\operatorname{Spec}C\to X$. An ideal $y$ of $C$ is assumed maximal (`hy`) and to contain $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the image $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   For an automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ and $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, the predicate [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) says: for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ viewed inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$, every integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ of $f,g$ with $p_g\ne0$, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the $\iota$-image of the expansion of $\tau x$ multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`; thus $\tau$ realises the action of $\gamma^{-1}$ on the modular curve. Such a $\tau$ is called a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ below.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is the local rigidity assumption for the model. It requires: for every point $z$ of $X$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ which is the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` (`hϖz`) and lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk (`hz`), and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y')=z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the same supersingularity condition as `hss` for the ideal $y'$ (`hss'`), there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal), a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f-\bigl(X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1\bigr)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the difference from [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ at its maximal ideal onto $S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v-f\,u\bigr)$, such that, writing $toC$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $mkS$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $germY$ for the composite of the canonical identification of the sections of $\mathcal O_X$ over the image of $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with $C$ and the germ map at $z$, the following seven clauses hold: (1) for every $a\in A$, $e$ carries the image of $a$ in the completed stalk to $mkS(C(\sigma a))$; (2) for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$; (3) for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (4) for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwines the action of $\tau$ on $C$ through $e\circ toC\circ germY$; $\theta$ fixes $mkS(C(w))$ for all $w\in W$; $\theta(mkS(X_j))-mkS\bigl(\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i\bigr)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $mkS(X_0),mkS(X_1)$; $c^{q+1}-1\in\mathfrak m_W$; $M_{ij}-c\,\gamma_{ij}\in\mathfrak m_W$ for all $i,j$; if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ then $c-1\in\mathfrak m_W$; and if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity then $c-1\notin\mathfrak m_W$; (5) for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ such that neither contains both $mkS(X_0)$ and $mkS(X_1)$, both contain $mkS(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and $P_i$ contains the class of $C(a_i)X_0+C(b_i)X_1+h_i$ for some $h_i\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e\circ toC$ are distinct; (6) for every prime $P$ of $S$ not containing both $mkS(X_0)$ and $mkS(X_1)$, containing $mkS(C(\sigma\varpi))$ and containing the class of $C(1)X_0+C(0)X_1+h$ for some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a\in C$: $toC(germY\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ is the image of an element of $\mathfrak m_A$; (7) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant with $t$ replaced by $t^{q\ell}$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the difference of that element and $a_0$ in $y'$, an exponent $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b\in W$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$ the sum $\sum_{i\le e_0}\operatorname{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^i b^{\,e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e\bigl(toC(germY(\text{that element}-a_0))\bigr)=mkS\,h$.
--
--   The statement then fixes such a configuration: a point $z$ of $X$, an element $\varpi_z$ of its stalk with `hϖz` and `hz`, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with `hy'` and the supersingularity condition `hss'`, together with `hy'y : y'.asIdeal = y`; and it fixes data $W_1$ (a complete discrete valuation domain), $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the completed stalk at $z$ onto $S:=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$. The hypothesis `hW₁` asserts exactly the conjunction of the seven clauses (1)–(7) above for these data $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ at the point $z$ and the point $y'$.
--
--   The remaining data are as follows. An ideal $J$ of $C$ is given, and `hJ` states that $J$ is the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $\operatorname{comap}_{\tau}\bigl(\operatorname{comap}_{e_1\circ toC\circ germY}(\,(mkS(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)),mkS(X_0),mkS(X_1))\,)\bigr)$, taken over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, where $\tau$ is used through its restriction to $C$. A subalgebra $B$ of $K$ over $A$ is given with `hB`: $B$ is the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x\in K:\exists i\in J,\ x\,\varpi_t=i\}$, with scalars restricted to $A$; thus $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ is given with `hBW`: $B\subseteq W$. Three further groups of hypotheses concern $B$ and $W$: `hR1` says $C\le B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$; `hR2` says $A\to B$ is formally smooth, of finite presentation, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` has five clauses: an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$; and an element of $K$ lies in $W$ exactly when it is $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses) concerns the special fibre: (a) for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the polynomial ring in two variables over the residue field modulo the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q` $-\,1$) whose kernel is the set of $b\in B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, which is compatible with $A\to$ residue field on scalars, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, there is a unit $c$ of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ with $(\,$`redQ q γ`$,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,c)\mapsto\overline{\det g}\cdot c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho\circ\tau=$ `hAction` of that pair applied to $\rho$ on all $b\in B$ with $\tau b\in B$, and such that $c\ne1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (b) every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ maps $B$ into $B$; (c) for every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ such that every $b\in B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ satisfies $\tau b\in B$ and $\tau b\in Q$; (d) if $b\in B$ is such that $\tau b\in\mathfrak m_W$ for all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\tau b\in B$, then $\varpi\mid b$ in $B$; (e) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, if $\tau$ preserves $y$ on $C$ (in the sense that for $b\in C$ with $\tau b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ iff $\tau b\in y$) then $f\in W$ iff $\tau f\in W$, for all $f\in K$.
--
--   Finally a subring $O$ of $K$ is given with `hO`: there are $a\in J$ with nonzero image in $K$, and, setting $B_a$ to be the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x\in K:\exists i\in J,\ x\,a=i\}$ with scalars restricted to $A$, a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$, such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ inside $K$ (an $f\in K$ lies in $O$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$ and $h\notin P$), every element of $y$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B$ is not contained in $O$. Moreover $O\subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), and $C\subseteq O$ (`hCO`). The last hypothesis `hIgStab` is the stability of Igusa-type valuation rings: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that an element of $L$ lies in $V$ exactly when it comes from $A$, such that $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$, such that $C\subseteq V$, and such that some $c\in C$ has the property that the value at $c$ of every monic polynomial over $A$ lies in $V$ and is a unit of $V$, one has: for all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $f\in V$ iff $\tau f\in V$ for all $f\in K$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion asserts: for all $s,t\in C$ and $k\in\mathbb N$ with $s\,t=\varpi^k$ in $C$ (so $s$ divides a power of $\varpi$), for every $a\in J$ with nonzero image in $K$, for every maximal ideal $P$ of the $A$-algebra $B_a=C[J/a]$ described above, such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (an $f\in K$ lies in $O$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$ and $h\notin P$), and for every $N\in\mathbb N$ such that
--
--   (i) $s\,a^{-N}\in O$;
--
--   (ii) $s\,a^{-N}$, whenever it lies in $W$, is not in $\mathfrak m_W$, i.e. is a unit of $W$;
--
--   (iii) for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that an element of $L$ lies in $V$ exactly when it comes from $A$, and such that $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$ whenever it lies in $V$, the following holds: if $j\in V$ and the value at $j$ of every monic polynomial over $A$ is a unit of $V$ whenever it lies in $V$, and if $O\subseteq V$, then $s\,a^{-N}$, whenever it lies in $V$, is not in $\mathfrak m_V$;
--
--   then $a^{N}s^{-1}\in O$.
--
--   A unit criterion at an end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart: an element $s\,a^{-N}$ of $K$ built from a divisor $s$ of a power of the uniformiser and from the blow-up coordinate $a\in J$, which is a unit of the exceptional valuation ring $W$ and of every Igusa-type valuation ring containing the local ring $O$ of the end, is shown to be invertible in $O$ itself. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_verticalUnit_pow_centre_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_verticalUnit_pow_centre_of_end_blowupChart) in the analysis of the local structure of the integral model at supersingular points.
